---
Encode input as base64 (standard alphabet, with padding).

Examples:
  ubertool base64 encode "hello"
  echo -n hello | ubertool base64 encode
  ubertool base64 encode "hello" --json
  printf 'alice\nbob\n' | ubertool base64 encode --batch

Usage: ubertool base64 encode [OPTIONS] [INPUT]

Arguments:
  [INPUT]
          Literal input to encode (omit to read from --in or stdin)

Options:
      --in <IN_PATH>
          Read input from file

      --json
          Output as JSON to stdout. Human messages still go to stderr

      --out <OUT_PATH>
          Write encoded output to file. If absent, output goes to stdout

  -q, --quiet
          Bare values only (pipe-friendly)

      --batch
          Read one item per line from stdin and emit JSONL (one record per line)

  -v, --verbose
          Verbose progress to stderr

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
